<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antonio da Sangallo the Younger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1484">1484</a>–<a href="/years/1546">1546</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antonio da Sangallo the Younger was a Florentine architect of the High <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a>, active mainly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. He designed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palazzo-farnese">Palazzo Farnese</a> for Cardinal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-paul-iii">Alessandro Farnese</a>, later Pope Paul III, served as chief architect of St Peter's Basilica and built fortifications for the Papal States, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fortezza-da-basso">Fortezza da Basso</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>. For the Farnese he also worked on their new capital at Castro.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antonio-da-sangallo-the-younger.jpg" alt="Antonio da Sangallo the Younger" width="320" height="194" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karelj · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Apostolic_Palace_model.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
